WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.421
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.721 --> 00:00:07.806
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.106 --> 00:00:14.497
Unit twenty-four: Starting a Business. In this unit, you will talk about business ideas and possible results.

4
00:00:15.483 --> 00:00:16.519
entrepreneur.

5
00:00:17.219 --> 00:00:20.275
entrepreneur means a person who starts their own business.

6
00:00:20.575 --> 00:00:23.167
Many young entrepreneurs start online shops.

7
00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:26.450
Your turn. Say: entrepreneur.

8
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.290
entrepreneur.

9
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:32.145
start-up.

10
00:00:32.845 --> 00:00:34.938
start-up means a new small company.

11
00:00:35.238 --> 00:00:37.376
Her start-up sells healthy snacks.

12
00:00:38.076 --> 00:00:40.357
Your turn. Say: start-up.

13
00:00:43.057 --> 00:00:44.116
start-up.

14
00:00:45.117 --> 00:00:46.187
business plan.

15
00:00:46.887 --> 00:00:50.965
business plan means a document describing how a business will work and make money.

16
00:00:51.265 --> 00:00:53.996
Investors always ask to see your business plan.

17
00:00:54.696 --> 00:00:57.221
Your turn. Say: business plan.

18
00:00:59.921 --> 00:01:01.061
business plan.

19
00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:03.016
investor.

20
00:01:03.716 --> 00:01:07.469
investor means a person who gives money to a business to get a profit.

21
00:01:07.769 --> 00:01:10.233
An investor gave them ten thousand dollars.

22
00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:13.179
Your turn. Say: investor.

23
00:01:15.879 --> 00:01:16.915
investor.

24
00:01:17.917 --> 00:01:18.953
profit margin.

25
00:01:19.653 --> 00:01:23.498
profit margin means the percentage of money you keep after costs.

26
00:01:23.798 --> 00:01:26.123
Coffee shops can have a high profit margin.

27
00:01:26.823 --> 00:01:29.254
Your turn. Say: profit margin.

28
00:01:31.954 --> 00:01:33.246
profit margin.

29
00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.425
customer base.

30
00:01:36.125 --> 00:01:40.261
customer base means the group of people who regularly buy from a business.

31
00:01:40.561 --> 00:01:42.886
Their customer base is mainly students.

32
00:01:43.586 --> 00:01:46.192
Your turn. Say: customer base.

33
00:01:48.892 --> 00:01:50.218
customer base.

34
00:01:51.217 --> 00:01:52.032
marketing.

35
00:01:52.732 --> 00:01:56.612
marketing means activities that help sell a product, like advertising.

36
00:01:56.912 --> 00:01:59.887
They spend most of their budget on social media marketing.

37
00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:02.880
Your turn. Say: marketing.

38
00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:06.581
marketing.

39
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:08.515
competitor.

40
00:02:09.215 --> 00:02:12.190
competitor means a business that sells similar things.

41
00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:15.104
Our main competitor is opening a shop next door.

42
00:02:15.804 --> 00:02:18.039
Your turn. Say: competitor.

43
00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:21.693
competitor.

44
00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:24.729
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:25.029 --> 00:02:27.435
I'm thinking of starting a coffee start-up.

46
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:33.504
Interesting! If you open near the university, you'll have a big customer base.

47
00:02:34.817 --> 00:02:36.607
But there are many competitors there.

48
00:02:37.917 --> 00:02:41.449
If I were you, I would focus on something different, like healthy drinks.

49
00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:45.841
If I found an investor, I would open a bigger shop.

50
00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:51.265
First, write a business plan. If it's clear, investors will listen.

51
00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:55.780
Grammar focus: First vs second conditional.

52
00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.601
Use the first conditional for real or likely situations.

53
00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:03.630
Use the second conditional for imaginary or unlikely situations.

54
00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:10.692
For example: If I save enough, I will open a shop. If I won the lottery, I would start a big company.

55
00:03:10.992 --> 00:03:14.304
Choose the conditional according to how likely the situation is.

56
00:03:15.317 --> 00:03:18.166
Now read and listen. From Market Stall to Brand.

57
00:03:18.466 --> 00:03:22.892
Ten years ago, Sreymom sold homemade chilli sauce at a small market stall.

58
00:03:24.183 --> 00:03:27.564
Her customer base grew quickly because her sauce tasted unique.

59
00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.533
She wrote a business plan and found an investor who believed in her.

60
00:03:33.817 --> 00:03:37.372
Today, her products are sold in supermarkets across the country.

61
00:03:38.683 --> 00:03:42.982
She says that if young entrepreneurs work hard, they will find their own success.

62
00:03:44.283 --> 00:03:46.611
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:46.911 --> 00:03:49.781
A person who starts their own business is an blank.

64
00:03:50.081 --> 00:03:53.572
A, investor. B, entrepreneur. C, competitor.

65
00:03:57.583 --> 00:03:59.548
The answer is B: entrepreneur.

66
00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.119
If it blank tomorrow, we'll stay at home.

67
00:04:03.419 --> 00:04:06.469
A, rains. B, rained. C, will rain.

68
00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.332
The answer is A: rains.

69
00:04:13.817 --> 00:04:16.490
If I blank a millionaire, I would travel the world.

70
00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:19.735
A, am. B, were. C, will be.

71
00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.308
The answer is B: were.

72
00:04:26.817 --> 00:04:29.420
A business that sells similar things is a blank.

73
00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.652
A, competitor. B, customer base. C, start-up.

74
00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.452
The answer is A: competitor.

75
00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:44.296
According to the text, Sreymom started by selling blank.

76
00:04:44.596 --> 00:04:48.482
A, coffee. B, chilli sauce. C, clothes.

77
00:04:52.483 --> 00:04:54.924
The answer is B: chilli sauce.

78
00:04:56.417 --> 00:05:00.184
Now it's your turn to speak. If you started a business, what would it be?

79
00:05:05.484 --> 00:05:10.455
If I started a business, I would open a small café with healthy drinks near a university.

80
00:05:10.755 --> 00:05:12.267
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:13.283 --> 00:05:17.468
Great work today! You learned eight new words and first vs second conditional.

82
00:05:17.768 --> 00:05:21.198
Today's value is hard work. Work hard and never give up.

83
00:05:21.498 --> 00:05:24.720
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

84
00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:27.811
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

